      "content": "Here's a revised version of the methodology section, incorporating more advanced terminology to increase the technical density:\n\n\"We will implement a targeted CRISPR-Cas9 genome editing strategy, leveraging the AAV9 vector as a highly efficient and stable delivery system to introduce precise, site-specific mutations into the HBB gene. By utilizing a low-pass sequencing approach and automated live-cell reporter gene (RoS4) analysis, we will assess the efficacy of the gene editing maneuver, enabling endothelial cell-specific disruption of the segmental chromosomal integrated allele. To validate gene editing outcomes, we will utilize multi-dimensional flow cytometry and RNA fluorescence in situ hybridization (FISH) techniques, facilitating the detection of gene expression and cellular fusion events, as well as high-resolution analysis of chromosomal architecture.\"",
